    "fileId": 29769,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Diagnostic criteria and differential diagnosis for lymphomatoid papulosis (LyP) {29719017}</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Werner Kempf",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.1pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Subtype </span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">(proportion of LyP cases)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Phenotype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 222.55pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"297\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Diagnostic histopathological and genetic criteria</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Differential diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Discriminating features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">A</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">(80%)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD4+, CD8&minus;, CD30+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 222.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"297\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Wedge-shaped infiltrate with scattered or small clusters of large pleomorphic CD30+ cells (sometimes multinucleated or Reed&ndash;Sternberg&ndash;like) and numerous inflammatory cells, i.e. small lymphocytes, neutrophils, and/or eosinophils <span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\">{7104214; 10845893; 15096372}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mycosis fungoides, tumour stage</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical evolution with preceding patches and plaques</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Hodgkin lymphoma (almost always secondary cutaneous involvement)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Staging: nodal involvement</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">C-ALCL</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical presentation: rapidly growing large tumour or multifocal nodules; cohesive sheets of large CD30+ T&nbsp;cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.1pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">B</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">(&lt;&nbsp;5%)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD4+, CD8&minus;, CD30+/&minus;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 222.55pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"297\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Epidermotropic infiltrate of small atypical CD30+ or CD30&minus; cells with cerebriform nuclei</span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> {7104214; 10845893; 15096372}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mycosis fungoides, patch/plaque stage</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical presentation with patches and plaques</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">C</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">(10%)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD4+, CD8&minus;, CD30+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 222.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"297\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Monotonous infiltrate with cohesive sheets of large CD30+ T&nbsp;cells; few admixed inflammatory cells<span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"> {7104214; 10845893; 15096372}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">C-ALCL</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical presentation: rapidly growing large tumour or multifocal nodules</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mycosis fungoides, tumour stage with large-cell transformation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical evolution with preceding patches and plaques; variable expression of CD30</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"FR\">Adult T-cell leukaemia/lymphoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Detection of HTLV-1/2, geographical clustering</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.1pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">D</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">(&lt;&nbsp;5%)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD4&minus;, CD8+, CD30+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 222.55pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"297\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Strongly epidermotropic, sometimes pagetoid infiltrate of atypical small to medium-sized CD8+, CD30+ pleomorphic T&nbsp;cells </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{20661014}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Primary cutaneous CD8+ aggressive epidermotropic cytotoxic T-cell lymphoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical presentation: rapidly evolving erosive or ulcerated plaques and nodules</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD8+, CD30&minus; (rarely CD30+)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD45RA+ (70%)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Pagetoid reticulosis (mycosis fungoides subtype)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical presentation: solitary erythematous and scaly lesion</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Various phenotypes including expression of CD8 and CD30</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">E</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">(&lt;&nbsp;5%)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD4&minus;, CD8+, CD30+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 222.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"297\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Angioinvasive infiltrates of mostly medium-sized CD8+, CD30+ pleomorphic cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Vascular occlusion, haemorrhages, extensive necrosis, and ulceration <span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\">{23026936}</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Note:</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Clinically, patients present with a few papulonodular lesions that rapidly ulcerate and evolve into large, necrotic, eschar-like lesions <span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\">{23026936}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Extranodal NK/T-cell lymphoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Staging: systemic involvement</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Association with EBV (LMP, EBER+)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cutaneous gamma-delta T-cell lymphoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical presentation: rapidly evolving erosive or ulcerated plaques and nodules</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Often CD56+ CD30&minus; (occasionally CD30+)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">TCR&gamma;&delta;+, TCR&alpha;&beta;&minus;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">C-ALCL (angioinvasive form)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical presentation: rapidly growing large tumour with ulceration</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD4+ or CD8+, CD30+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.1pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">LyP with <em>DUSP22</em> locus rearrangement</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">(&lt;&nbsp;5%)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"109\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CD8+ or CD4/CD8 double-negative, CD30+</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 222.55pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"297\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Biphasic pattern: epidermotropic, small to medium-sized, weakly CD30+ T&nbsp;cells with cerebriform nuclei, and a dense dermal infiltrate of strongly CD30+ medium-sized to large atypical cells </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{23648461}</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Defining criterion: chromosomal rearrangements involving the <em>DUSP22</em>-<em>IRF4</em> locus on 6p25.3 </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{37127078}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 152.8pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"204\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mycosis fungoides, tumour stage with large-cell transformation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.65pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"216\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical evolution with preceding patches and plaques; variable expression of CD30</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">C-ALCL, primary cutaneous anaplastic large cell lymphoma; EBER, EBV-encoded small RNA.</span></p>",
